.TH GITISH 1 2026-10-18 "gitish 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.\" Left-aligned and unhyphenated, so key names and paths copy as written.
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
gitish \- a terminal git staging UI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gitish
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gitish
is \fBgit add \-p\fR, but interactive.
It shows the changed files of a repository on the left and the hunks of the selected
file on the right.
You stage, unstage and discard single hunks or whole files, resolve merge conflicts,
write a commit message and commit, and push or pull, without leaving the terminal.
.PP
It opens the repository found by searching upwards from the current directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-path \fIpath\fR
Open the repository at, or above,
.I path
instead of the current directory.
.TP
.B \-\-open \fIstate\fR
Start in a UI state.
.I state
is
.B theme\-picker
or
.BR spinner .
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help, \-?
Print a short help and exit.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
The keys are fixed. What a key does depends on the mode and on the focused panel.
Press
.B ?
in the program for the full list.
.TP
.B q, Ctrl\-c, Ctrl\-q
quit; close an overlay.
.TP
.B j, Down
move down.
.TP
.B k, Up
move up.
.TP
.B n
next hunk or conflict.
.TP
.B p
previous hunk or conflict.
.TP
.B Tab
switch panel.
.TP
.B s
stage file or hunk.
.TP
.B u
unstage file or hunk.
.TP
.B d
discard hunk.
.TP
.B X
delete untracked file.
.TP
.B o
resolve conflict: ours.
.TP
.B i
resolve conflict: incoming.
.TP
.B b
resolve conflict: both.
.TP
.B c
open the commit bar.
.TP
.B P
push.
.TP
.B L
pull.
.TP
.B t
theme picker.
.TP
.B ?
help overlay.
.TP
.B r
refresh.
.TP
.B Enter
confirm; next field.
.TP
.B Esc
cancel; close.
.TP
.B Backspace
delete a character.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gitish/config.toml
Settings. A missing file is not an error, and every key is optional.
A file that cannot be parsed is copied to
.I config.toml.bak
and the defaults are used.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gitish/themes/
base16 YAML themes. The four Catppuccin themes are written here on first run.
Any base16 file in the folder appears in the theme picker.
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B theme
The name of the active theme, a string. The theme picker saves it.
.TP
.B transparent
When true, gitish uses the terminal's own background. Default
.BR false .
.TP
.B use_nerd_fonts
When true, icons are Nerd Font glyphs. When false they are plain ASCII.
Default
.BR true .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1)
